(Case Title: Whitaker v. Orion Logistics Inc.) Tj
T*
(Case Number: 2025-CV-4412) Tj
T*
(Court: United States District Court, Eastern District of Texas) Tj
T*
(Date: June 18, 2025) Tj
T*
(Plaintiff: Elena Whitaker) Tj
T*
(Defendant: Orion Logistics Inc.) Tj
T*
()Tj
T*
(Summary:) Tj
T*
(Plaintiff Elena Whitaker filed suit against Orion Logistics Inc.) Tj
T*
(alleging wrongful termination and unpaid overtime wages under the) Tj
T*
(Fair Labor Standards Act following her dismissal on April 2, 2025.) Tj
T*
()Tj
T*
(Background:) Tj
T*
(Whitaker worked as a freight coordinator for Orion Logistics from) Tj
T*
(March 2021 until April 2025. She alleges she regularly worked 55) Tj
T*
(hours per week but was compensated only for 40 hours. After she) Tj
T*
(reported the discrepancy to the Department of Labor, she was) Tj
T*
(terminated within eleven days of filing that complaint.) Tj
T*
()Tj
T*
(Legal Arguments:) Tj
T*
(Plaintiff's Claims:) Tj
T*
(Retaliation: Termination followed protected whistleblower activity.) Tj
T*
(Unpaid Overtime: Orion failed to pay time-and-a-half for 15 hours) Tj
T*
(of weekly overtime across approximately 210 weeks of employment.) Tj
T*
()Tj
T*
(Defendant's Defense:) Tj
T*
(Orion argues Whitaker was an exempt administrative employee and) Tj
T*
(that her termination resulted from documented performance issues) Tj
T*
(unrelated to the Department of Labor complaint.) Tj
T*
()Tj
T*
(Court Decision:) Tj
T*
(The court ruled in favor of the plaintiff on both counts. The court) Tj
T*
(found the eleven-day gap between the complaint and the termination) Tj
T*
(established a prima facie case of retaliation that Orion failed to) Tj
T*
(rebut, and that Whitaker did not meet the administrative exemption.) Tj
T*
()Tj
T*
(Final Judgment:) Tj
T*
(Orion Logistics Inc. is ordered to pay Elena Whitaker $148,500 in) Tj
T*
(back wages, liquidated damages, and attorney fees within 45 days.) Tj
T*
(Case Closed.) Tj
T*
